  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="5">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IIIEg">III Eg</ref> 5</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="5" corresp="#wit-g-a">⁊ sece man hundredgemót, swa hit ǽr geset wæs.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="5" corresp="#wit-a">⁊ sece mon hundredgemót, swa hit ær geset wæs.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="5" corresp="#wit-g2">⁊ sece man hundredes gemot, swa hit ær geset wæs.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="5" corresp="#wit-q">Et requiratur hundretum, sicut antea fuit institutum.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="5" corresp="#wit-d">[Be gemotum.] [Ld] ⁊ sece man hundredes gemot swa hit ǽr geset wæs.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-d">And the hundred court shall be attended as has been previously ordained.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">(Von Gerichtsversammlungen. Ld) Und man besuche das Hundertgericht, wie es zuvor festgesetzt worden ist.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">(Of court-meetings. Ld) And let the hundred-court be attended, as was established before.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann compares Hu 1.</note>
      </div>
    </body>
  </text>
